Algorithms
    Metaphone and Double Metaphone were designed by Lawrence Philips.
    Metaphone was published in Computer Language 7(12), 1990.
    Double Metaphone was published, with C++ code, in C/C++ Users
    Journal 18(6), June 2000.

R/double_metaphone.R
    The rules are a translation into R of the C implementation of Double
    Metaphone by Maurice Aubrey (Copyright 2000, Maurice Aubrey), which
    is based on Lawrence Philips' C++ code and includes bug fixes by
    Kevin Atkinson. Aubrey's code is distributed under the same terms as
    Perl, which allow redistribution under the GNU General Public
    License. The same C code is used in the R package 'PGRdup'
    (Copyright ICAR-NBPGR, GPL-2 | GPL-3) by J. Aravind, J. Radhamani,
    Kalyani Srinivasan, B. Ananda Subhash and co-authors,
    which brought Double Metaphone to R and inspired this package.
    Unlike that code, this version does not cut the codes to four
    characters.

